Stitch all test periods together → realistic equity curve

In layman terms:
1. You test your strategy for a specific window and filter out the best strategy with the best metrics
2. Using that same strategy, apply it to the years ahead of what you previously tested to see if the edge is genuine or not
3. Not to not change the paramters of the strategy you're walking forward with

